                "retweet_count": 52,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Investing in our communities means tackling our biggest challenges with meaningful solutions\u2014investing in public safety, behavioral health, housing, and community programs.\n\nOver the last several years, we\u2019ve brought home millions in funding for public safety and behavioral health programs, including a new clinic in the International District, a sobering center in Albuquerque, housing and addiction recovery on the West Side, and a proposal for a first-of-its-kind behavioral health and resource center in Sandoval County in Bernalillo.\u00a0 We\u2019re delivering millions for technology and tools to help local law enforcement and first responders address crime and get drugs off the streets and new fire and emergency response centers in the East Mountains, Sandia Pueblo, and Valencia County.  And, we\u2019ve brought home millions for affordable housing for families, seniors, and young people, Albuquerque\u2019s first youth homeless shelter, and our first transitional housing campus for veterans.\u00a0\n\nThis is the work we do every day in our office.  Not sound bites, but sustained and dedicated investment in our communities and families and in transformational projects to help those who are struggling most.",
